<title>RUSSIA: Caspian Pipeline Consortium signs &quot;final&quot; deal.</title>
<headline>Caspian Pipeline Consortium signs &quot;final&quot; deal.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Caspian Pipeline Consortium (CPC), planning to build an oil pipeline from Kazakhstan to Russia, signed on Friday what it calls a &quot;final agreement&quot; on the deal.</p>
<p>Russian Energy Minister Boris Nemtsov told the signing ceremony that the CPC pipeline was a unique way of bringing competition to Russia's monopoly oil transport business, run by Transneft.</p>
</text>
